# keystore2 for recovery. Overrides TWRP's copy.
#
# [!] writepid /dev/cpuset/foreground/tasks REMOVED. Recovery does not mount the
# cgroup hierarchy, so init logged
#   init: cpuset cgroup controller is not mounted!
#   init: failed to write pid to files: couldn't write N to /dev/cpuset/foreground/tasks
# on every restart. Harmless in itself, but it is noise on top of the real
# failure and there is nothing for it to write to.
#
# [!] The `interface` line is required, not decorative. Without it servicemanager
# cannot lazy-start keystore2 and logs, once per second, forever:
#   servicemanager: Since 'android.system.keystore2.IKeystoreService/default'
#     could not be found, trying to start it as a lazy AIDL service
#   init: Control message: Could not find
#     'aidl/android.system.keystore2.IKeystoreService/default' for
#     ctl.interface_start
# while TWRP sits in waitForService() and never draws its UI.
#
# It is ALSO declared in /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml: IKeystoreService is a
# VINTF-stability binder, so servicemanager rejects the registration outright
# without a manifest entry and keystore2 panics with
#   Failed to register service ... because of UNKNOWN_ERROR
# The two requirements are separate and both are mandatory.
on late-init
    start keystore2

service keystore2 /system/bin/keystore2 /tmp/misc/keystore
    interface aidl android.system.keystore2.IKeystoreService/default
    class early_hal
    user root
    group keystore readproc log
    seclabel u:r:recovery:s0
